    verification recorderRefusalCannotCiteTheVerifiersWritesLineRetroGate : Test { :>> id = "e724b9bf-51e9-4069-a66c-afe0c0c77323"; :>> title = "Sprint 744 retro gate (autonomous, D0049)"; :>> createdAt = "2026-09-18"; :>> createdBy = "claudeFable5"; :>> method = VerificationMethod::analyze; :>> procedureText = "Written at close-out, before the verifier is dispatched; avoidable issues scanned (issue011), each finding a tracked item or the reason it is not. (1) D0516 was recorded with a decision text enumerating (1)(2)(3) and the record decision write accepted it; only keel gate guard, run minutes later, named it COMPOUND under D0303 - the write path does not run clause_count, so a compound Decision can land in the tree and be committed by a session that skips the guard. Tracked: issue604 (Low), resolved by dcRecordDecisionRefusesACompoundText (record decision refuses a text whose clause_count is 2 or more at the write, D0303). (2) The relabel is enforced only by skill text: a verifier that still writes OWED WRITES is not refused by any check, since the checker reads the recorder's report and not the receipt. Not tracked as its own item: D0516 states the residual, and the eighth refusal catches the misread from the recorder's side whichever label the receipt used. (3) The sprint 735 first report was recovered from the transcript, not from a file the recorder had written - a recorder report lives only in the subagent's reply. Not tracked: the recorder brief already requires the report written to <ABS SCRATCH PATH>/recorder-report.txt, and sprint 735's was; the fixture was cut from the reply because the scratchpad file had been overwritten by the second dispatch. No new control. (4) Found by this sprint's first verifier: its receipt was green on every rung but filed DISCREPANCIES against lib=true because the test-verify skill's receipt table said lib is true only when a keel-cli/src path changed; touched.rs line 575 (members/keel-suite) sets lib whenever stems is non-empty, and .engine changes contribute init (issue530), so the receipt was honest and the skill row was the defect. Fixed at the root in the same commit: the row now states the code's rule and cites the line. Not tracked as its own item: the source-reference guard (D0514) now holds the citation the row carries, so a drift of that line is red; the rule text itself has no checker, and that residual is stated here. The verifier was re-dispatched against the corrected tree."; }
